Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: program the SCU XSI selection before bringup

phylink only invokes ->pcs_pre_config() from phylink_major_config(), and
phylink_major_config() is skipped whenever the link is driven by an
attached PHY (MLO_AN_PHY) and the interface does not change.  On the
AN4475-G2 the gdm4 combo port has a phy-handle, so the interface stays
2500BASE-X for the whole uptime and airoha_pcs_setup_scu() is never
executed.

Consequence on hardware: AIROHA_SCU_SSR3 (0x1fa20094) keeps
ETH_XSI_SEL = 0, the SerDes lane is not routed to the HSGMII PCS, and
the PCS receiver sees no signal at all:

  pcs_pma DIG_RO_RESERVE_2 (0x1fa7b380) RX_SIGDET = 0

Writing ETH_XSI_SEL = AIROHA_SCU_ETH_XSI_HSGMII (0x4000) by hand flips
RX_SIGDET to 1 immediately, which proves the SCU selection is the
missing piece and that the lane itself is healthy.

->pcs_config() does run (it is called on every link up), so program the
SCU there as well.  It must happen before the analog bringup, because
the PLL/CDR calibration depends on the lane actually being routed.

Signed-off-by: local

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-airoha.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-airoha.c
@@ -465,9 +465,20 @@ static int airoha_pcs_config(struct phylink_pcs *pcs, unsigned int neg_mode,
 	maps = &priv->maps[port->index];
 	port->interface = interface;
 	data = priv->data;
 
+	/*
+	 * phylink only runs ->pcs_pre_config() from phylink_major_config(),
+	 * which is skipped when a PHY is attached and the interface never
+	 * changes.  ETH_XSI_SEL then stays 0, the SerDes lane is never
+	 * routed to this PCS, RX_SIGDET reads 0 and nothing is received
+	 * even though the copper side reports link up.  Program the SCU
+	 * here too, and before the analog bringup so that the PLL/CDR
+	 * calibration runs with the lane already routed.
+	 */
+	airoha_pcs_setup_scu(priv, port->index, interface);
+
 	/* Apply Analog and Digital configuration for PCS */
 	if (data->bringup) {
 		ret = data->bringup(priv, index, interface);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;